From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: declare the true payload length

**Needs exynos-modem with "sit: pad request payloads to a multiple of 8".**

That change makes the builder pad a request's payload the way the vendor
RIL does, while the header's `length` keeps declaring the true size. Four
payloads here were pre-padded to the size stock puts on the wire, so they
declared the padding as payload and the length field came out too big:

    0x0247  24 -> 18    [u8 aid_len][aid, 16][u8 p2]
    0x020f  32 -> 26 + data
    0x020e   8 -> 4     [u32 ch]
    0x0d17  24 -> 19

Those are exactly the `+0x004` divergences the parity report had against
stock -- A=1e/P=24 for 0x0247, A=28/P=2c for 0x020f, A=10/P=14 for 0x020e,
A=1f/P=24 for 0x0d17 -- and the declared sizes are the layouts already
documented in the comments beside them.

The test peers have to drain the padding or they desync. They read exactly
`length` bytes off the socketpair and then take the next header, so once
frames are padded the leftover bytes get read as a header and the id
assertion fires. A read_padding() helper beside read_all() drains it, and
all six body-reading peers call it. This is needed for the padding change
alone, independent of the four payload sizes.
